            }
          ],
          "type": "RETURN"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Choose Breakdown Dimension"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778057000008"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_BREAKDOWN_DIMENSION_SELECTOR",
          "id": "1776127459716",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776127459718_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Objective\n\nProduce the full COA breakdown request state for the current analytic-view data fetch.\n\nThis node returns semantic input for a later code node. Do not call tools and do not format a final answer.\n\n## Input\n\nCurrent user message:\n<USER_MESSAGE>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</USER_MESSAGE>\n\nChat history:\n<CHAT_HISTORY>{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}</CHAT_HISTORY>\n\nPrior breakdown array:\n<PRIOR_BREAKDOWN>{{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}</PRIOR_BREAKDOWN>\n\nAvailable breakdown dimensions:\n<AVAILABLE_DIMENSIONS>{{$context.$variables.lastUsedQueryResponse.metadata.chartOfAccounts}}</AVAILABLE_DIMENSIONS>\n\n## Output Shape\n\nReturn JSON only. Do not wrap in Markdown. Do not include comments.\n\n{\"breakdowns\":[{\"dimensionName\":\"<dimension name>\",\"expandLevel\":\"1\",\"memberNames\":[]}]}\n\nField rules:\n- breakdowns: array containing the complete appropriate COA breakdown state for this fetch, not just newly requested dimensions.\n- dimensionName: the segment key from AVAILABLE_DIMENSIONS.segments, such as vFCompany.\n- expandLevel: string \"1\" for ordinary one-level breakdown; string \"-1\" for leaf/detail/lowest-level/all-descendants requests.\n- memberNames: member names or member codes for that dimension. Use an empty array when no specific members apply. Numeric member codes may remain numbers.\n\n## Dimension Rules\n\n- Use only dimensions that should apply to the current fetch after considering the current user message, chat history, and PRIOR_BREAKDOWN.\n- If the user asks to add a breakdown, include prior breakdown dimensions that still apply plus the new requested dimensions.\n- If the user asks to remove or clear a breakdown dimension, omit that dimension from the returned array.\n- Do not return dimensions that are only part of the base query scope unless the user asks to break down, drill, group, expand, or show contributors by that dimension.\n- Choose dimensionName only from the keys of AVAILABLE_DIMENSIONS.segments.\n- Match the user's requested dimension against each segment's key, label, and qualifiers.\n- If a requested dimension is not present in AVAILABLE_DIMENSIONS.segments, omit it from breakdowns.\n- If the requested dimension is ambiguous, omit it from breakdowns. Do not guess.\n- Always return the segment key as dimensionName, not the display label.\n\nCommon breakdown phrases:\n- break down by\n- breakdown by\n- split by\n- group by\n- drill down by\n- expand by\n- contributors by\n- children by\n- detail by\n- leaf by\n- by <dimension> when used with a balance or subledger amount request\n\n## Expand Level Rules\n\n- Default to \"1\".\n- Use \"-1\" only when the user explicitly asks for leaf, detail, lowest level, full detail, all descendants, or complete drilldown.\n- Apply the requested level only to the dimension it modifies.\n- If the user requests multiple dimensions with one shared level phrase, apply that level to all requested dimensions.\n- If a dimension is carried forward from PRIOR_BREAKDOWN and the user does not change its level, preserve the prior level.\n\n## Member Rules\n\n- memberNames should include only member names/codes that apply to the breakdown dimension.\n- If the user lists multiple members for one dimension, preserve order and remove duplicates.\n- If the user explicitly gives member codes or values, return those codes/values.\n- If chat history shows a displayed member as <value> - <description> and the user references that description, return only <value>.\n- Resolve descriptions to values only from exact or unambiguous matches in chat history. Do not resolve descriptions from model knowledge.\n- If the user refers to displayed results indirectly, such as above companies, these products, or shown cost centers, do not invent values from chat history. Return the dimension with memberNames: [].\n- If a dimension is carried forward from PRIOR_BREAKDOWN and the user does not change its members, preserve the prior members.\n\n## Non-Breakdown Cases\n\nIf the current user message has no active COA breakdown request and no prior breakdown should be preserved, return:\n{\"breakdowns\":[]}\n\n## Examples\n\n- Break that down by company -> {\"breakdowns\":[{\"dimensionName\":\"vFCompany\",\"expandLevel\":\"1\",\"memberNames\":[]}]}\n- Expand account 5000 and 6000 -> {\"breakdowns\":[{\"dimensionName\":\"vFAccount\",\"expandLevel\":\"1\",\"memberNames\":[5000,6000]}]}\n- Show detail by company 200 and cost center 300 -> {\"breakdowns\":[{\"dimensionName\":\"vFCompany\",\"expandLevel\":\"-1\",\"memberNames\":[200]},{\"dimensionName\":\"vFCostCenter\",\"expandLevel\":\"-1\",\"memberNames\":[300]}]}\n- Break down by account and cost center -> {\"breakdowns\":[{\"dimensionName\":\"vFAccount\",\"expandLevel\":\"1\",\"memberNames\":[]},{\"dimensionName\":\"vFCostCenter\",\"expandLevel\":\"1\",\"memberNames\":[]}]}\n\n## Hard Rules\n\n- Output valid JSON only\n- Output exactly one object\n- Include exactly one top-level key: breakdowns\n- No string-form breakdowns\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"breakdowns\"],\"properties\":{\"breakdowns\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"dimensionName\",\"expandLevel\",\"memberNames\"],\"properties\":{\"dimensionName\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"expandLevel\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"memberNames\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}}}}}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Set Breakdown Dimension"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778055785200"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_SET_FIELDS_SET_BREAKDOWN_DIMENSION",
          "id": "1776224314096",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776224321259",
              "name": "coaBreakdown",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_BREAKDOWN_DIMENSIONS.$output.result.breakdowns}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Determine Subledger Object"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778040214049"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_OBJECT_SELECTOR",
          "id": "1778040214047",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778040214047_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict object selector for a Payables Subledger Supporting Assistant in the Oracle Fusion Financials General Ledger and Subledger Accounting context.\n\nYour job is to select the single best summary or detail object from $CANDIDATES for the current in-domain Payables request.\n\nReturn exactly one integer and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order.\n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n$PRIOR_CONTEXT:\n{\n  priorSelectedSubledgerName: {{$context.$variables.selectedSubledgerName}},\n  priorRequestType: {{$context.$variables.requestType}},\n  priorAnalyticView: {{$context.$variables.previousAnalyticViewNameUsed}},\n  priorBusinessView: {{$context.$variables.previousBusinessViewNameUsed}}\n}\n\n$CANDIDATES:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.promptText}}\n\n## Selection Rules\n\n1. Use only the listed candidates.\n2. Return a valid zero-based candidate index only when a listed candidate is sufficiently supported by the current request and relevant prior context.\n3. Return -1 when no listed candidate is sufficiently supported. Do not ask for clarification.\n4. Treat every request as in-domain for Payables. Do not reject it for unsupported subledgers.\n5. Choose a SUMMARY object when the request asks for aggregate, grouped, rolled-up, total, count, activity, or breakdown output.\n6. Choose a DETAIL object when the request asks to list, show, retrieve, display, or view transaction-level, invoice-level, payment-level, receipt-level, line-level, distribution-level, or accounting-entry-level rows.\n7. Prefer the candidate whose description, important attributes, and selection hints best match the request.\n8. Use $CHAT_HISTORY and $PRIOR_CONTEXT only to resolve follow-up context. Explicit user input has priority over prior context.\n9. If the prior analytic view or business view matches one listed candidate and the latest message is an underspecified follow-up, prefer that prior candidate unless the latest message clearly implies another listed candidate.\n   - Treat a presentation-only sort/order follow-up as underspecified and retain the prior candidate unless the current message explicitly names a different business subject or grain.\n10. Do not switch objects based on weak or generic wording. Switch only when the current request clearly names or strongly implies another candidate.\n11. If multiple candidates seem plausible and no prior matching candidate should be carried forward, choose the most specific sufficiently supported fit; otherwise return -1.\n12. For unqualified Payables transaction requests, treat \"transactions\" as invoice-oriented Payables activity, not payment activity.\n13. For unqualified summary requests about Payables transactions, supplier transactions, transaction totals, transaction activity, or accounted amount, choose Payables Accounted Transaction Summary.\nFor unqualified summary requests about discount, discounts, discount taken, discounts taken, discount amount, or discount amounts, especially by supplier, choose Payables Accounted Transaction Summary. Do not choose Payables Accounted Payment Summary solely because discount language appears; choose a payment object only when the latest request explicitly centers on payments or payment attributes.\n14. For unqualified detail requests about Payables transactions, supplier transactions, transaction rows, or transaction accounting detail, choose Payables Accounted Invoice Detail.\n15. Choose Payables Accounted Payment Summary or Payables Accounted Payment Detail only when the latest request explicitly centers on payments, payment method, payment status, payment number, bank account, cleared payments, reconciled payments, future-dated payments, refunds, or cash disbursement activity.\n16. Choose Payables Accounted Prepayment Application Detail only when the latest request specifically asks about prepayment applications or applying prepayments to invoices.\n\n## Output Rules\n\n- Output exactly one integer.\n- The integer must be either a valid zero-based index from $CANDIDATES or -1.\n- Return -1 when no listed candidate is sufficiently supported.\n- No JSON object.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanation.\n- No trailing text.\n- No nulls."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"integer\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Determine Analytic View Flow Requirements"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778057000009"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYTIC_VIEW_FLOW_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1776969594318",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776969594323_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a selected-object flow requirement detector for a Subledger Supporting Assistant in Oracle Fusion Financials.\n\nYour job is to determine, in one pass, whether the current request needs:\n1. a query-scope rebuild,\n2. a Chart of Accounts breakdown step, and\n3. custom sorting.\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order.\n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n$TURN_CONTEXT:\n{\n  selectedHierarchies: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.state?.domainSlice?.shared?.hierarchy?.hierarchyOverrides || $context.$triggers.REST.$input.state?.shared?.hierarchy?.hierarchyOverrides || []}}\n}\n\n$ACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  priorSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.previousAnalyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.previousBusinessViewNameUsed}},\n  priorRequestType: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.requestType}},\n  activeSubledgerQuery: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedQueryResponse}},\n  activeSubledgerQueryData: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedDataResponse}},\n  availableSortFields: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.lastUsedDataKeyOrder}},\n  activeSortBy: {{$context.$variables.sortBy}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\n$CURRENT_OBJECT:\n{{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}}\n\n$CURRENT_REQUEST_TYPE:\n{{$context.$variables.requestType}}\n\n## scopeChanged Rules\n\nSet `scopeChanged` to true when any of the following is true:\n- $ACTIVE_STATE.priorRequestType is empty, missing, or different from $CURRENT_REQUEST_TYPE\n- $ACTIVE_STATE is empty, missing, or unusable\n- $CURRENT_OBJECT is empty or differs from $ACTIVE_STATE.priorSubledgerObject\n- the current request adds, removes, or changes a concrete filter, qualifier, named member value, hierarchy override, non-COA grouping, or detail grain\n- the current request introduces or changes a supplier, customer, account, company, cost center, ledger, period, currency, business unit, payment, receipt, invoice, transaction, or other filter-bearing value\n- the current request asks to clear, remove, or reset sorting\n- the current request adds or changes a top/bottom/first/last N, row limit, or result-count limit, because the query row limit must be regenerated\n- an explicitly requested sort field is not represented in $ACTIVE_STATE.availableSortFields and query regeneration is needed to project it\n\nSet `scopeChanged` to false only when the current and prior request type and selected object are the same, active filters and detail grain are preserved, hierarchy selections still match, and the request is either:\n- only a sort/order change that can be applied to the active result, or\n- for a SUMMARY request only, a COA breakdown, grouping, expansion, or drill-depth change without a new concrete member value.\n\nFor DETAIL requests, any change other than a presentation-only sort/order change requires `scopeChanged: true`.\n\n## breakdownRequired Rules\n\nSet `breakdownRequired` to true only for a SUMMARY request that asks for grouped, expanded, or drilled-down output on a COA segment, including:\n- breakdown by account, company, cost center, intercompany, or another COA segment\n- drill into or expand by a COA segment\n- lowest-level, leaf-level, detailed, or child-level COA breakdown\n\nSet `breakdownRequired` to false for:\n- DETAIL requests\n- totals or aggregates without COA grouping\n- grouping by a non-COA dimension such as supplier, customer, business unit, period, or legal entity\n- sort-only requests\n\n## sortRequired Rules\n\nSet `sortRequired` to true only when the current user message explicitly asks to sort, order, rank, reorder, append a sort key, reverse the active sort, or clear sorting.\n\nSet `sortRequired` to false when the current message contains no explicit sorting instruction. Prior active sorting is preserved downstream when it remains applicable.\n\n## sortAction Rules\n\n- `none`: no explicit sorting instruction in the current message\n- `replace`: establish a new sort definition or change the active sort\n- `append`: add secondary sort keys to the active sort; recognize phrases such as `then by`, `also by`, `add`, `include`, `secondary sort`, and `next sort key`\n- `clear`: remove, clear, or reset active sorting\n\nUse `clear` only with `sortRequired: true`, `sortBy: []`, and `scopeChanged: true`.\n\n## sortBy Rules\n\n- Include only sort fields explicitly requested in the current message, except that `reverse the current sort` may reuse $ACTIVE_STATE.activeSortBy when it is non-empty\n- Preserve the user's field order\n- Each item must be `{\"field\":\"<field>\",\"order\":\"asc|desc\"}`\n- Default an omitted direction to `asc`\n- Descending cues include descending, desc, Z-A, highest, largest, greatest, latest, newest, and most recent\n- Ascending cues include ascending, asc, A-Z, lowest, smallest, least, oldest, and earliest\n- For a follow-up such as `then by accounting date descending`, return only that current field with `sortAction: \"append\"`\n- For `reverse the current sort`, preserve the active field order and invert each active direction; if there is no active sort, do not invent a field\n- Use exact active output aliases from $ACTIVE_STATE.availableSortFields when they are unambiguous\n- Do not invent, guess, or arbitrarily choose among ambiguous fields such as generic `date`, `status`, `number`, or `amount`\n- Use an empty array when `sortRequired` is false or `sortAction` is `clear`\n\n## Interaction Between Fields\n\n- `scopeChanged`, `breakdownRequired`, and `sortRequired` are independent\n- A filter change plus sorting has `scopeChanged: true` and `sortRequired: true`\n- A same-object sort-only request can have `scopeChanged: false` and `sortRequired: true`\n- A SUMMARY COA-breakdown-only request can have `scopeChanged: false`, `breakdownRequired: true`, and `sortRequired: false`\n- An explicit sort takes precedence over implicit COA-breakdown ordering\n\n## Examples\n\n- `Sort by supplier` on an active result:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":false,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":true,\"sortAction\":\"replace\",\"sortBy\":[{\"field\":\"supplier\",\"order\":\"asc\"}]}`\n- `Then by accounted amount descending`:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":false,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":true,\"sortAction\":\"append\",\"sortBy\":[{\"field\":\"accounted amount\",\"order\":\"desc\"}]}`\n- `Remove sorting`:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":true,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":true,\"sortAction\":\"clear\",\"sortBy\":[]}`\n- A same-object filter change plus `sort by accounting date latest first`:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":true,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":true,\"sortAction\":\"replace\",\"sortBy\":[{\"field\":\"accounting date\",\"order\":\"desc\"}]}`\n- `Show the top 5 by accounted amount`:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":true,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":true,\"sortAction\":\"replace\",\"sortBy\":[{\"field\":\"accounted amount\",\"order\":\"desc\"}]}`\n- `Break down by account` for an active SUMMARY:\n  `{\"scopeChanged\":false,\"breakdownRequired\":true,\"sortRequired\":false,\"sortAction\":\"none\",\"sortBy\":[]}`\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly:\n{\"scopeChanged\":true|false,\"breakdownRequired\":true|false,\"sortRequired\":true|false,\"sortAction\":\"none|replace|append|clear\",\"sortBy\":[{\"field\":\"<field>\",\"order\":\"asc|desc\"}]}\n\n## Hard Rules\n\n- Output valid JSON only\n- Output exactly one object\n- Include exactly the keys `scopeChanged`, `breakdownRequired`, `sortRequired`, `sortAction`, and `sortBy`\n- Boolean fields must be booleans\n- `sortAction` must be one of `none`, `replace`, `append`, or `clear`\n- `sortBy` must be an array\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"scopeChanged\",\"breakdownRequired\",\"sortRequired\",\"sortAction\",\"sortBy\"],\"properties\":{\"scopeChanged\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"breakdownRequired\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"sortRequired\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"sortAction\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"none\",\"replace\",\"append\",\"clear\"]},\"sortBy\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"field\",\"order\"],\"properties\":{\"field\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"order\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"asc\",\"desc\"]}}}}}}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Rephrase Business View Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777619990223"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_REPHRASE_BUSINESS_VIEW_REQUEST",
          "id": "1776970051652",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776970051652_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a question rephraser for a Subledger Supporting Assistant.\n\nYour job is to:\n1. Build a single fully constrained natural-language userQuestion\n2. Build a concise export-friendly queryTitle for the same request\n\nYou must output exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order. \n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n$ACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  priorSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.previousAnalyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.previousBusinessViewNameUsed}} ,\n  currentSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}} ,\n  activeSubledgerQuery: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedQueryResponse}} ,\n  activeSubledgerQueryData: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedDataResponse}} ,\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}},\n  activeSortBy: {{$context.$variables.sortBy}}\n}\n\n## Goal\nProduce a complete self-contained userQuestion that preserves the current request plus any still-active context from prior turns, and a concise title suitable for export/data extract display.\n\n## userQuestion Construction Rules\n\nBuild userQuestion as a complete natural-language question that can be sent downstream without additional narration.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve all user-specified active filters, entities, dimensions, periods, currencies, ledger references, supplier/customer references, and transaction qualifiers that still apply\n- If the current message is a follow-up, merge it with relevant prior context\n- Keep the wording semantically equivalent to the user’s intent\n- When rephrasing based on chart of account members, prefer the value over the description\n- Do not retain filters that only appear in the query / data but are not mentioned by the user in the current turn or prior turns\n- You may improve grammar and word order only\n- Do not add explanations, interpretation, or extra business terms\n- Do not generalize or specialize user terms\n- Do not rewrite or reinterpret text inside single or double quotes\n- Do not drop user-specified values unless the user explicitly removes them\n- Before returning, verify that no active supplier, customer, account, company, cost center, ledger, period, currency, identifier, or hierarchy override constraint was dropped unless the user explicitly removed or replaced it\n- Do not include raw technical context fields such as chartOfAccountsId, processExecutionId, conversationId, or raw Context JSON unless the user explicitly asked about them\n- Do not include literal analytic-view or business-view object names or identifiers in userQuestion, including selected object technical names, display names, or values from workflow state. Describe the business subject in user-facing terms instead\n- Preserve user-specified ledger and hierarchy constraints in the generated query intent using natural language.\n- Do not add ledger or hierarchy constraints that only appear in raw workflow state.\n- Do not include raw hierarchy override JSON, technical IDs, or implementation details.\n- Preserve the current message's explicit sort fields, their order, and their ascending or descending directions\n- When the current message adds a secondary sort, include both the still-active prior sort and the new secondary sort in the rephrased question\n- Preserve an active prior sort only when the prior and current Subledger objects are the same and the user did not replace, contradict, clear, or remove it\n- If the user clears or removes sorting, omit the prior sort and the clear/remove instruction from userQuestion so downstream query generation receives an otherwise complete request with no sorting\n- Do not carry sorting across a Subledger object or request-grain change\n\n## queryTitle Construction Rules\n\nBuild queryTitle as a short, user-facing title for data extract/export.\n\nRequirements:\n- Make it concise and descriptive\n- Preserve the main business subject, object, and strongest visible filters such as period, supplier/customer, account, company, transaction identifier, journal, batch, or detail grain when important\n- Do not include raw technical context fields, JSON, BQL, chartOfAccountsId, processExecutionId, conversationId, or implementation details\n- Do not include literal analytic-view or business-view object names or identifiers in queryTitle, including selected object technical names, display names, or values from workflow state. Use a business-subject title instead\n- Do not wrap the title in quotes unless the quote is part of a business value\n- Prefer a compact noun phrase over a full sentence\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object with this shape:\n{\"userQuestion\":\"<fully constrained natural-language question>\",\"queryTitle\":\"<concise export title>\"}\n\n## Hard Rules\n- Output valid JSON only\n- Output exactly one object\n- Include exactly the keys userQuestion and queryTitle\n- Both values must be strings\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"userQuestion\",\"queryTitle\"],\"properties\":{\"userQuestion\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"queryTitle\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Check for Header-Only Business View Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776227970807"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_HEADER_ONLY_BUSINESS_VIEW_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1776970051653",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776970051653_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a detector for a Subledger Supporting Assistant that determines whether a business-view request should include header-only data.\n\nYour job is to:\n1. Determine includeHeaderOnly as a boolean\n\nYou must output exactly one boolean value and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order. \n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n$ACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  priorSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}} ,\n  activeSubledgerQuery: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedQueryResponse}} ,\n  activeSubledgerQueryData: {{$context.$variables.lastUsedDataResponse}} ,\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\n## Goal\nDetermine whether the request is asking for summary/header-level data only or line-level/accounting-distribution detail.\n\n## includeHeaderOnly Rules\n\nSet includeHeaderOnly to true when the user is asking for summary or header-level information only, including cases like:\n- show\n- list\nwhen the user does not explicitly ask for line-level, distribution-level, accounting-entry-level, detail, or details intent\n\nSet includeHeaderOnly to false only when the user explicitly asks for line-level or accounting/distribution detail, including concepts such as:\n- invoice lines\n- transaction lines\n- payment lines\n- distribution lines\n- tax details\n- distributions\n- accounting entries\n- account combinations\n- CCID\n- natural account\n- segments\n- line amounts\n- quantities\n- detail\n- details\n\nDocument numbers alone do not force includeHeaderOnly = false. Mentions of invoice numbers, payment numbers, prepayment numbers, credit memo numbers, debit memo numbers, or other Payables document identifiers should remain header-only unless the user explicitly asks for detail, details, line, distribution, accounting-entry, segment, CCID, natural-account, line amount, or quantity detail.\n\nIf the request does not explicitly ask for line-level or accounting/distribution detail, prefer includeHeaderOnly = true.\n\nUse $ACTIVE_STATE and $CHAT_HISTORY only to resolve follow-up references where the latest message is underspecified.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly:\ntrue|false\n\nwith the actual boolean value of includeHeaderOnly.\n\n## Hard Rules\n- Output exactly one boolean value\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Prepare Business View Rephrased Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const asObject = (value) =>\n  value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\nconst asString = (value) => (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\");\nconst parseRephraseOutput = (value) => {\n  if (asObject(value)) {\n    const userQuestion = asString(value.userQuestion) || asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n    const res = {\n      userQuestion,\n      queryTitle: asString(value.queryTitle) || userQuestion\n    };\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    const raw = value.trim();\n    if (raw) {\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n        if (asObject(parsed)) {\n          const userQuestion = asString(parsed.userQuestion) || raw;\n          const res = {\n            userQuestion,\n            queryTitle: asString(parsed.queryTitle) || userQuestion\n          };\n          return res;\n        }\n      } catch (error) {\n        // Fall through to legacy plain-text handling.\n      }\n    }\n    const userQuestion = raw || asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n    const res = {\n      userQuestion,\n      queryTitle: userQuestion\n    };\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  const userQuestion = asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n  const res = {\n    userQuestion,\n    queryTitle: userQuestion\n  };\n  return res;\n};\n\nreturn parseRephraseOutput($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_REPHRASE_BUSINESS_VIEW_REQUEST?.$output);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776227970807"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_PREPARE_BUSINESS_VIEW_REPHRASED_REQUEST",
          "id": "1777619990223",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
