          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_BUSINESS_VIEW_MULTI_OBJECT_RETRIEVAL_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1778290894159",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778290894159_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict multi-object retrieval classifier for a Payables Subledger Supporting Assistant detail query.\n\nYour job is to decide whether the current business-view data retrieval should expand across multiple Payables subledger detail objects.\n\nReturn exactly one boolean value and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order.\n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n$SELECTED_BUSINESS_VIEW:\n{{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}}\n\n## Rules\n\nDefault to false.\n\nEvaluate this only after business-view selection. This flag is independent of business-view selection. Do not change or second-guess the selected business view.\n\nSet the result to true when the latest user request asks broadly for Payables subledger activity across transaction types and does not identify a single specific transaction type. Strong examples include wording such as supplier transactions, Payables transactions, supplier activity, invoices and payments together, or transactions at the Payables subledger level.\n\nSet the result to true when the business view was selected from underspecified or fallback context and the latest user request does not contain a clear Payables transaction type keyword.\n\nSet the result to false when the latest user request identifies a specific Payables transaction type, including invoice, invoices, payment, payments, credit memo, debit memo, prepayment, prepayment application, refund, refunds, future-dated payment, future-dated payments, reconciled payment, or reconciled payments.\n\nUse $CHAT_HISTORY only to resolve underspecified follow-up references. Explicit current user input has priority over prior context.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly:\ntrue|false\n\n## Hard Rules\n\n- Output exactly one boolean value\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Parse Business View Multi-Object Retrieval",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_BUSINESS_VIEW_MULTI_OBJECT_RETRIEVAL_CLASSIFIER.$output;\n\nconst text = typeof rawOutput === \"boolean\"\n  ? String(rawOutput)\n  : typeof rawOutput === \"string\"\n    ? rawOutput.trim().toLowerCase()\n    : \"\";\n\nconst expandSubledgerBvData = text === \"true\" ? true : text === \"false\" ? false : false;\n\nconst res = { expandSubledgerBvData };\n\nreturn res;"
          },
