          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778290894160"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYTIC_VIEW_MULTI_OBJECT_RETRIEVAL_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1778290894158",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778290894158_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict multi-object retrieval classifier for a Payables Subledger Supporting Assistant summary query.\n\nYour job is to decide whether the current analytic-view data retrieval should expand across paired Payables subledger transaction summary objects.\n\nReturn exactly one boolean value and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order.\n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n$SELECTED_ANALYTIC_VIEW:\n{{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}}\n\n## Rules\n\nDefault to false.\n\nEvaluate this only after analytic-view selection. This flag is independent of analytic-view selection. Do not change or second-guess the selected analytic view.\n\nSet the result to true when the latest user request asks broadly for Payables subledger activity across transaction types and does not identify a single specific transaction type. Strong examples include wording such as supplier transactions, Payables transactions, supplier activity, invoices and payments together, or transactions at the Payables subledger level.\nSet the result to true for unqualified summary requests about discount, discounts, discount taken, discounts taken, discount amount, or discount amounts when no specific Payables transaction type is identified. Treat supplier-level discount-taken questions, such as asking how much discount was taken from each supplier, as broad Payables subledger activity for multi-object expansion.\n\nSet the result to false when the latest user request identifies a specific Payables transaction type, including invoice, invoices, payment, payments, credit memo, debit memo, prepayment, prepayment application, refund, refunds, future-dated payment, future-dated payments, reconciled payment, or reconciled payments.\n\nUse $CHAT_HISTORY only to resolve underspecified follow-up references. Explicit current user input has priority over prior context.\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly:\ntrue|false\n\n## Hard Rules\n\n- Output exactly one boolean value\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Parse Analytic View Multi-Object Retrieval",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYTIC_VIEW_MULTI_OBJECT_RETRIEVAL_CLASSIFIER.$output;\n\nconst text = typeof rawOutput === \"boolean\"\n  ? String(rawOutput)\n  : typeof rawOutput === \"string\"\n    ? rawOutput.trim().toLowerCase()\n    : \"\";\n\nconst expandSubledgerData = text === \"true\" ? true : text === \"false\" ? false : false;\n\nconst res = { expandSubledgerData };\n\nreturn res;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776221365742"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_MULTI_OBJECT_RETRIEVAL",
          "id": "1778290894160",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Rephrase User Question"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777619990222"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_REPHRASE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_REQUEST",
          "id": "1776969882238",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776969882245_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a question rephraser for a Subledger Supporting Assistant.\n\nYour job is to:\n1. Build a single fully constrained natural-language userQuestion\n2. Build a concise export-friendly queryTitle for the same request\n\nYou must output exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs\n\n$CHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n$CHAT_HISTORY is ordered in chronological order. \n\n$USER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n$ACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  priorSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.previousAnalyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.previousBusinessViewNameUsed}} ,\n  currentSubledgerObject: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed || $context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}} ,\n  activeSortBy: {{$context.$variables.sortBy}}\n}\n\n\n## Goal\nProduce a complete self-contained userQuestion that preserves the current request plus any still-active context from prior turns, and a concise title suitable for export/data extract display.\n\n## userQuestion Construction Rules\n\nBuild userQuestion as a complete natural-language question that can be sent downstream without additional narration.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve all user-specified active filters, entities, dimensions, periods, currencies, ledger references, supplier/customer references, and breakdown/grouping requests that still apply\n- If the current message is a follow-up, merge it with relevant prior context\n- Keep the wording semantically equivalent to the user’s intent\n- When rephrasing based on chart of account members, prefer the value over the description\n- Do not retain filters that only appear in the query / data but are not mentioned by the user in the current turn or prior turns\n- You may improve grammar and word order only\n- Do not add explanations, interpretation, or extra business terms\n- Do not generalize or specialize user terms\n- Do not rewrite or reinterpret text inside single or double quotes\n- Do not drop user-specified values unless the user explicitly removes them\n- Before returning, verify that no active supplier, customer, account, company, cost center, ledger, period, currency, identifier, or hierarchy override constraint was dropped unless the user explicitly removed or replaced it\n- Do not include raw technical context fields such as chartOfAccountsId, processExecutionId, conversationId, or raw Context JSON unless the user explicitly asked about them\n- Do not include literal analytic-view or business-view object names or identifiers in userQuestion, including selected object technical names, display names, or values from workflow state. Describe the business subject in user-facing terms instead\n- Preserve user-specified ledger and hierarchy constraints in the generated query intent using natural language.\n- Do not add ledger or hierarchy constraints that only appear in raw workflow state.\n- Do not include raw hierarchy override JSON, technical IDs, or implementation details.\n- Preserve the current message's explicit sort fields, their order, and their ascending or descending directions\n- When the current message adds a secondary sort, include both the still-active prior sort and the new secondary sort in the rephrased question\n- Preserve an active prior sort only when the prior and current Subledger objects are the same and the user did not replace, contradict, clear, or remove it\n- If the user clears or removes sorting, omit the prior sort and the clear/remove instruction from userQuestion so downstream query generation receives an otherwise complete request with no sorting\n- Do not carry sorting across a Subledger object or request-grain change\n\n## queryTitle Construction Rules\n\nBuild queryTitle as a short, user-facing title for data extract/export.\n\nRequirements:\n- Make it concise and descriptive\n- Preserve the main business subject, object, and strongest visible filters such as period, supplier/customer, account, company, or breakdown when important\n- Do not include raw technical context fields, JSON, BQL, chartOfAccountsId, processExecutionId, conversationId, or implementation details\n- Do not include literal analytic-view or business-view object names or identifiers in queryTitle, including selected object technical names, display names, or values from workflow state. Use a business-subject title instead\n- Do not wrap the title in quotes unless the quote is part of a business value\n- Prefer a compact noun phrase over a full sentence\n\n## Output Schema\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object with this shape:\n{\"userQuestion\":\"<fully constrained natural-language question>\",\"queryTitle\":\"<concise export title>\"}\n\n## Hard Rules\n- Output valid JSON only\n- Output exactly one object\n- Include exactly the keys userQuestion and queryTitle\n- Both values must be strings\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"userQuestion\",\"queryTitle\"],\"properties\":{\"userQuestion\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"queryTitle\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1778057000005",
            "name": "Prepare Analytic View Rephrased Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const asObject = (value) =>\n  value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\nconst asString = (value) => (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\");\nconst parseRephraseOutput = (value) => {\n  if (asObject(value)) {\n    const userQuestion = asString(value.userQuestion) || asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n    const res = {\n      userQuestion,\n      queryTitle: asString(value.queryTitle) || userQuestion\n    };\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    const raw = value.trim();\n    if (raw) {\n      try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n        if (asObject(parsed)) {\n          const userQuestion = asString(parsed.userQuestion) || raw;\n          const res = {\n            userQuestion,\n            queryTitle: asString(parsed.queryTitle) || userQuestion\n          };\n          return res;\n        }\n      } catch (error) {\n        // Fall through to legacy plain-text handling.\n      }\n    }\n    const userQuestion = raw || asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n    const res = {\n      userQuestion,\n      queryTitle: userQuestion\n    };\n    return res;\n  }\n\n  const userQuestion = asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\n  const res = {\n    userQuestion,\n    queryTitle: userQuestion\n  };\n  return res;\n};\n\nreturn parseRephraseOutput($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_REPHRASE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_REQUEST?.$output);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776221365742"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_PREPARE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_REPHRASED_REQUEST",
          "id": "1777619990222",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
